  "worked_solution": "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}5f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =5{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5\\cdot ⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5e,\\,-5{e}^{2},\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
